{
  "name": "Encorp | Homework | Week 03 | HW 05 | Support Ticket Router Intake",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Support Ticket Router - 1/2 Intake (Week 03 / HW 05)\nTicket Form -> Prepare Ticket -> Analyze Urgency (Sentiment Analysis) -> Classify Department (Text Classifier) -> Department * -> Build Ticket Record -> Save Ticket As Pending (Data Table) -> Compose Review Email -> Send Review Request (Gmail)\n\nThis workflow ENDS after the e-mail. It does not wait for the human. The workflow \"Support Ticket Router Review\" (2/2) continues when the reviewer opens the link and submits the review form.\n\n**Coverage:** R1 Ticket Form + Prepare Ticket | R2 Analyze Urgency (Urgent / Frustrated / Neutral / Positive) | R3 Classify Department (Sales / Technical / Billing / General; \"Other\" goes to General) | R4 (part 1) Save Ticket As Pending + Send Review Request.\n\n**What changed vs. the first plan, and why**\n- Send and Wait was replaced by two workflows: no execution is parked in \"Waiting\" and the human has no deadline.\n- The ticket state lives in the Data Table support_tickets (pending_review -> reviewed -> processed | failed). It can be queried and updated by ticketId, uses no Sheets API quota and does not touch the Sheet columns required by the task. The Google Sheet keeps only results (tab Tickets) and history (tab Audit Log).\n- The reviewer gets a link to a form, not one-click buttons: mail scanners open links and could confirm a ticket by accident.\n- ticketId = date + random suffix ($execution.id is not reliable in test runs).\n\n**Setup:** connect OpenRouter and Gmail credentials | create Data Table support_tickets (columns in test-data/data-table-schema.md) | in Prepare Ticket set reviewFormUrl (production URL of the Review Form from workflow 2/2) and reviewerEmail | publish workflow 2/2 first.",
        "height": 470,
        "width": 1500,
        "color": 7
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -100,
        -560
      ],
      "id": "dfc96501-7f6e-4828-82b6-5c3beaea80cb",
      "name": "Sticky Note Overview"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 1. Intake (R1)\nA ticket enters through a form. Prepare Ticket normalises the fields, creates ticketId and receivedAt and holds the two settings (reviewFormUrl, reviewerEmail).",
        "height": 400,
        "width": 440,
        "color": 4
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -80,
        130
      ],
      "id": "08e67f3e-f6ac-4371-a4b4-021dc2700e63",
      "name": "Sticky Note Group 1"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 2. AI classification (R2, R3)\nOne OpenRouter model serves both nodes (temperature 0). Analyze Urgency has 4 outputs and Classify Department has 4 + Other: every output is wired on, so no ticket is lost. Each Department node sets the department; Other is treated as General.",
        "height": 760,
        "width": 780,
        "color": 5
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        480,
        -20
      ],
      "id": "730a11ae-e079-4398-8370-4fd0b638774a",
      "name": "Sticky Note Group 2"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 3. State and notification (R4, part 1)\nBuild Ticket Record fixes the AI sentiment (sentimentAi) and status = pending_review. Save Ticket As Pending stores the full ticket in the Data Table - the source of truth for the review. Send Review Request e-mails the ticket (HTML-escaped) and the link to the review form.",
        "height": 400,
        "width": 1100,
        "color": 6
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1300,
        130
      ],
      "id": "3aac6406-8130-407b-8a8e-4783cde746c2",
      "name": "Sticky Note Group 3"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Design improvement (NOT built): workflow 3 \"Pending Review Reminder\"\nA Schedule Trigger (e.g. hourly) reads the Data Table support_tickets where status = pending_review, keeps tickets older than N hours (receivedAt) and sends one reminder e-mail with the list and the review links; after M hours it escalates to a second reviewer.\nPossible extensions: column remindedAt (no repeated reminders), SLA by sentiment (Urgent 1 h, Frustrated 4 h, others 24 h), a daily report of tickets with status failed.\nThis is the reason the state is kept in a Data Table: with Send and Wait pending tickets are only \"Waiting\" executions that cannot be queried or reminded.",
        "height": 330,
        "width": 1100,
        "color": 3
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1300,
        560
      ],
      "id": "b3b18548-50d3-42e3-b40a-fc0d1f0037bb",
      "name": "Sticky Note Improvement"
    },
